   "source": [
    "# ✈️ Airline Passenger Satisfaction — CC105 Final Project\n",
    "\n",
    "**Student:** Mudrikal Al-Sharief  \n",
    "**Course:** CC105 — Machine Learning  \n",
    "**Dataset:** [Airline Passenger Satisfaction — Kaggle (TJ Mahal)](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/teejmahal20/airline-passenger-satisfaction)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📌 Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This project aims to **predict airline passenger satisfaction** (satisfied vs. neutral/dissatisfied) using machine learning classification models.  \n",
    "Instead of using all 26 columns, we narrow the focus to **8 high-impact features** that are:\n",
    "- Directly actionable for airlines (things they can improve)\n",
    "- Strongly correlated with satisfaction based on domain knowledge\n",
    "- Practical enough to present in a clean Django web app UI\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🎯 Selected Features\n",
    "| Feature | Type | Why It Matters |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Online Boarding | Ordinal (0–5) | Digital experience is a top satisfaction driver |\n",
    "| Inflight Wifi Service | Ordinal (0–5) | Connectivity strongly linked to modern traveler satisfaction |\n",
    "| Seat Comfort | Ordinal (0–5) | Physical comfort is always a key factor |\n",
    "| Cleanliness | Ordinal (0–5) | Hygiene correlates with overall experience |\n",
    "| Class | Categorical | Business vs Economy experience differs drastically |\n",
    "| Type of Travel | Categorical | Business travelers vs leisure travelers have different expectations |\n",
    "| Flight Distance | Numerical | Longer flights demand more from the airline |\n",
    "| Total Delay | Engineered | Combined departure + arrival delay (our engineered feature) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Target Variable:** `satisfaction` (Binary: satisfied / neutral or dissatisfied)"
   ]
  },
  {
