   "source": [
    "### 🔎 Observation: Missing Values\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset has **missing values in `Arrival Delay in Minutes`** (~310 records).  \n",
    "Since we will be engineering a `Total Delay` feature (Departure + Arrival Delay), we need to handle this before feature creation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Strategy:** Fill missing delay values with the **median** — robust to outliers (some flights have extreme delays).  \n",
    "We also drop `Unnamed: 0` (it's just an old row index from the CSV export) and remove exact duplicate rows."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-clean",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 🧹 Section 4: Data Cleaning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 117,
   "id": "cell-clean",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Duplicate rows removed: 0\n",
      "Missing values remaining: 310\n",
      "Final shape after cleaning: (103904, 24)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df = df_raw.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop the old index column\n",
    "if 'Unnamed: 0' in df.columns:\n",
    "    df.drop(columns=['Unnamed: 0'], inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fill missing delay values with median (robust to outliers)\n",
    "df['Departure Delay in Minutes'].fillna(df['Departure Delay in Minutes'].median(), inplace=True)\n",
    "df['Arrival Delay in Minutes'].fillna(df['Arrival Delay in Minutes'].median(), inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop duplicates\n",
    "before = len(df)\n",
    "df.drop_duplicates(inplace=True)\n",
    "after = len(df)\n",
    "print(f'Duplicate rows removed: {before - after}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Missing values remaining: {df.isnull().sum().sum()}')\n",
    "print(f'Final shape after cleaning: {df.shape}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-feature-eng",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## ⚙️ Section 5: Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.1 — Total Delay (New Feature)\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of keeping `Departure Delay` and `Arrival Delay` as two separate features (which would add noise for our Django UI), we combine them into a single, more meaningful feature: **Total Delay**.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Total Delay = Departure Delay in Minutes + Arrival Delay in Minutes**\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a classic **additive feature engineering** technique — it reduces dimensionality while preserving the combined impact of delays on satisfaction.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.2 — Delay Category (Bonus Engineered Feature)\n",
    "\n",
    "We also create a categorical bucketing of Total Delay to capture **non-linear effects**:  \n",
    "- `No Delay` (0 min) → passengers experience no inconvenience  \n",
    "- `Minor Delay` (1–30 min) → mild frustration  \n",
    "- `Moderate Delay` (31–60 min) → noticeable dissatisfaction  \n",
    "- `Major Delay` (60+ min) → strong negative impact on satisfaction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 118,
   "id": "cell-feature-eng",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "New features created:\n",
      "          Total Delay Delay Category\n",
      "count   103594.000000         103904\n",
      "unique            NaN              4\n",
      "top               NaN       No Delay\n",
      "freq              NaN          47459\n",
      "mean        29.926617            NaN\n",
      "std         76.149672            NaN\n",
      "min          0.000000            NaN\n",
      "25%          0.000000            NaN\n",
      "50%          2.000000            NaN\n",
      "75%         24.000000            NaN\n",
      "max       3176.000000            NaN\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Feature 1: Total Delay\n",
    "df['Total Delay'] = df['Departure Delay in Minutes'] + df['Arrival Delay in Minutes']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Feature 2: Delay Category (bonus ordinal bucketing)\n",
    "def categorize_delay(d):\n",
    "    if d == 0:\n",
    "        return 'No Delay'\n",
    "    elif d <= 30:\n",
    "        return 'Minor Delay'\n",
    "    elif d <= 60:\n",
    "        return 'Moderate Delay'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'Major Delay'\n",
    "\n",
    "df['Delay Category'] = df['Total Delay'].apply(categorize_delay)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('New features created:')\n",
    "print(df[['Total Delay', 'Delay Category']].describe(include='all'))"
   ]
  },
